@751 = ~Lightning~
@752 = ~Lightning (Invocation)
Level: 5
Range: visual range of the caster
Duration: instantaneous
Casting Time: 6
Area of Effect: one creature and a 3-meter radius around it
Saving Throw: half

The warlord calls upon the forces of nature to summon a lightning bolt that strikes the designated target. The spell must be cast outdoors, otherwise it will have no effect. On impact, the lightning deals 1D8 points of electrical damage per level of the warlord to the target and all the creatures within the area (max 20D8). A successful save vs. spell halves the damage.~
@75299 = ~Lightning (Invocation)
Level: 5
Range: visual range of the caster
Duration: instantaneous
Casting Time: 3
Area of Effect: 1 creature and 3-meter radius surrounding
Saving Throw: half

The warlord calls upon the forces of nature to summon a lightning bolt that strikes the designated target. The spell must be cast outdoors, otherwise it will have no effect. On impact, the lightning deals 20D8 points of electrical damage to the target and all the creatures within the area. A successful save vs. spell halves the damage.~

@753 = ~Mental Control~
@754 = ~Mental Control (Enchantment)
Level: 5
Range: visual range of the caster
Duration: 3 rounds + 1 round / 2 levels
Casting Time: 5
Area of Effect: one creature
Saving Throw: negates

The warlord who casts this spell tries to control the actions of the target.
If the target fails a save vs. spell at -4, it comes under the warlord's control and obeys his orders. It may turn against its own allies, but retains enough awareness to break the spell immediately if the warlord or any party member harms it.
If the creature is weak or unlucky enough to fail the save without the penalty, the bond created by the spell is much stronger. In such a case, the control over the creature is full, so the latter will not react if a party member tries to harm it, and only a successful dispel or expiration of the spell will free it from the clutches of the wizard.
This spell can only control intelligent humanoid creatures. The mental bond is telepathic, language and cultural differences pose no obstacle.~
@7541 = ~Mental Control (Enchantment)
Level: 5
Range: visual range of the caster
Duration: 13 rounds
Casting Time: 3
Area of Effect: one creature
Saving Throw: negates

The warlord who casts this spell tries to control the actions of the target.
If the target fails a save vs. spell at -4, it comes under the warlord's control and obeys his orders. It may turn against its own allies, but retains enough awareness to break the spell immediately if the warlord or any party member harms it.
If the creature is weak or unlucky enough to fail the save without the penalty, the bond created by the spell is much stronger. In such a case, the control over the creature is full, so the latter will not react if a party member tries to harm it, and only a successful dispel or expiration of the spell will free it from the clutches of the wizard.
This spell can only control intelligent humanoid creatures. The mental bond is telepathic, language and cultural differences pose no obstacle.~
@7542 = ~Under Control~

@755 = ~Charged Weapon~
@756 = ~Charged Weapon (Evocation)
Level: 5
Range: 0
Duration: 2 rounds
Casting Time: 5
Area of Effect: caster
Saving Throw: none

This spell charges the warlord's weapon with raw energy drawn from four elements: fire, cold, electricity, and acid. For 2 rounds, each hit deals an additional 8D4 points of damage, divided equally among the four elements. The energy is too unstable to remain in the weapon for more than a few seconds. After 2 rounds, the energy dissipates as the four elements oppose one another; there is a 5% chance that the energy erupts into a maelstrom, dealing 8d4 points of damage to the wielder and everyone nearby.~
@7561 = ~Charged Weapon (Evocation)
Level: 5
Range: 0
Duration: 2 rounds
Casting Time: 3
Area of Effect: caster
Saving Throw: none

This spell charges the warlord's weapon with raw energy drawn from four elements: fire, cold, electricity, and acid. For 2 rounds, each hit deals an additional 8D4 points of damage, divided equally among the four elements. The energy is too unstable to remain in the weapon for more than a few seconds. After 2 rounds, the energy dissipates as the four elements oppose one another; there is a 5% chance that the energy erupts into a maelstrom, dealing 8d4 points of damage to the wielder and everyone nearby.~
