Level: 5
Range: visual range of the caster
Duration: 2 rounds
Casting Time: 5
Area of Effect: one creature
Saving Throw: none

This spell charges the recipient's weapon with raw energy drawn from four elements: fire, cold, electricity, and acid. For 2 rounds, each hit deals an additional 8D4 points of damage, divided equally among the four elements. The energy is too unstable to remain in the weapon for more than a few seconds. After 2 rounds, the energy dissipates as the four elements oppose one another.

All allies within 5 meters of the recipient also benefit from reduced effects of the spell:
Their weapons are charged with four energies, each dealing 1d6 points of damage for 8 seconds.~

@758 = ~Heroism (Enchantment)
Level: 5
Range: 0
Duration: 5 rounds + 1 round / level
Casting Time: 6
Area of Effect: caster
Saving Throw: none

This spell gives the warlord the greatness and fortitude that makes heroes out of mere men. He gains a +2 bonus to attack rolls, saving throws and damage.
Other effects are added as the spellcaster gains power, according to the following table:
Level 11 : immunity to all forms of fear.
Level 13 : +10 additional temporary hit points.
Level 15 : immunity to charm, +1 charisma.
Level 17 : bonuses to attack rolls, saving throws and damage set at +3.
Level 19 : immunity to confusion.~
@7581 = ~Heroism (Enchantment)
Level: 5
Range: 0
Duration: 25 rounds
Casting Time: 3
Area of Effect: caster
Saving Throw: none

This spell gives the warlord the greatness and fortitude that makes heroes out of mere men. He gains a +3 bonus to attack rolls, saving throws and damage, 10 additional temporary hit points and 1 point of charisma, and is immune to any form of fear, charm and confusion.~
@7582 = ~Heroism (Enchantment)
