Stoneskin protects only against physical weapon damage. It does not prevent elemental damage if the hit is successful, and does not dispel destructive spells.

All allies within 5 meters of the recipient also benefit from reduced effects of the spell: 7 skins that they can keep for 4 turns.~

@7515 = ~Phantasmal Fist~
@7516 = ~Phantasmal Fist (Illusion)
Level: 5
Range: visual range of the caster
Duration: instantaneous
Casting Time: 5
Area of Effect: one creature
Saving Throw: negates

This spell offers the warlord an option against an opponent who resists his spells. He uses a crude but violent illusion to make the opponent BELIEVE it has been struck. Magic resistance offers no protection against this deception. The phantasmal fist creates above the victim a huge fist that strikes to crush him. If the victim instinctively believes it is being crushed, the psychic backlash inflicts 1D6 +1 points of damage per level of the warlord (Max 20D6 +20). A successful save vs. spell lets the victim recognize the illusion or believe it has dodged the blow, preventing all damage.~
@75161 = ~Phantasmal Fist (Illusion)
Level: 5
Range: visual range of the caster
Duration: instantaneous
Casting Time: 3
Area of Effect: one creature
Saving Throw: negates

This spell offers the warlord an option against an opponent who resists his spells. He uses a crude but violent illusion to make the opponent BELIEVE it has been struck. Magic resistance offers no protection against this deception. The phantasmal fist creates above the victim a huge fist that strikes to crush him. If the victim instinctively believes it is being crushed, the psychic backlash inflicts 20D6 +20 points of damage. A successful save vs. spell lets the victim recognize the illusion or believe it has dodged the blow, preventing all damage.~

@7517 = ~Draconic Strength~
@7518 = ~Draconic Strength (Transmutation, Enchantment)
Level: 5
Range: 0
Duration: 5 rounds + 1 round / 2 levels
Casting Time: 6
Area of Effect: caster
Saving Throw: none

The warlord discovered this unusual spell while seeking the power of a dragon. It partially transforms him without changing his appearance, filling his body with magical energy. He gains a dragon's Armor Class, Hit Dice and magic resistance, receiving 4 additional hit points for each Hit Die above his own. He also gains immunity to one element and half the dragon's combat modifier as a bonus to all melee damage.
In fact, the granted power while casting the spell is determined randomly by two die rolls, which vary according to the level of the mage:
Level 9 to 13 : 1D4
Level 14 to 18: 1D6
Level 19+     : 1D8

The first result determines the type of dragon:
1: White Dragon
2: Black Dragon
3: Copper Dragon
4: Blue Dragon
5: Bronze Dragon
6: Silver Dragon
7: Red Dragon
8: Gold Dragon

and the second determines the age of the dragon:
1: Juvenile
2: Young Adult
3: Adult
4: Mature Adult
5: Old
6: Very Old
7: Venerable
8: Wyrm

The transformed wizard does not create an aura of terror and gains neither a dragon's breath weapon nor its other special abilities.
Multiple Draconic Strength effects do not stack.~
