@7519 = ~Pulverization~
@7520 = ~Pulverization (Alteration)
Level: 5
Range: visual range of the caster
Duration: instantaneous
Casting Time: 5
Area of Effect: 10-meter radius
Saving Throw: special

When the warlord casts this spell, the soil at the targeted area heats up to its breaking point before exploding, throwing fire and burning embers on all nearby creatures. Each creature can be struck by one fragment per wizard level (max 17), each one inflicting 1D4 points of crushing damage and 1 point of fire damage. A save vs. spell avoids half the impacts.
The spell leaves a small crater. Only stone explodes; wood and flesh burn without exploding. Since the spell targets the ground rather than living creatures, magic resistance offers no protection.~
@75201 = ~Pulverization (Alteration)
Level: 5
Range: visual range of the caster
Duration: instantaneous
Casting Time: 3
Area of Effect: 10-meter radius
Saving Throw: special

When the warlord casts this spell, the soil at the targeted area heats up to its breaking point before exploding, throwing fire and burning embers on all nearby creatures. They suffer 17D4 points of crushing damage and 17 points of fire damage. A save vs. spell avoids half the impacts.
The spell leaves a small crater. Only stone explodes; wood and flesh burn without exploding. Since the spell targets the ground rather than living creatures, magic resistance offers no protection.~

@7521 = ~Regeneration~
@7522 = ~Regeneration (Necromancy)
Level: 5
Range: 0
Duration: 3 rounds / 2 levels
Casting Time: 6
Area of Effect: caster
Saving Throw: none

This powerful spell allows the warlord to accelerate natural regeneration of his body. Throughout the duration of the spell he recovers 1D4 hit points per round (without exceeding his maximum hit points). The power of this spell increases with caster experience, and regeneration grants 1D6 at level 15, and 1D4 +2 at level 20.~
